  "body": "### What is the issue with the Notifications API Standard?\n\n>User agents should not display [non-persistent notification](https://notifications.spec.whatwg.org/#non-persistent-notification) in a platform’s \"notification center\" (if available).\r\n\r\nI don't think anyone follows this, AFAIK every engine puts non-persistent notification to the notification center, including Firefox, Chrome, Safari on Windows and macOS.\r\n\r\n![Firefox and Chrome puts non-persistent notification to the Windows notification center](https://github.com/whatwg/notifications/assets/3396686/890ddc26-33aa-4154-aa76-ea057e3a2c65)\r\n\r\nI see no reason to not put it there as long as the triggering page is still open. It's added by 0005987711586c6bf2ed20a7e3f157db18a9e9b3, so perhaps @annevk may remember the background behind this.",
